{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.RivinConcavity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.RivinConcavity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.strictConcaveOn_tetVolLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.strictConcaveOn_tetVolLine","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L406-L419","doc":"**RIVIN CONCAVITY FOR ONE IDEAL TETRAHEDRON.**\n\n`Λ(α)+Λ(β)+Λ(γ)` is *strictly concave* along every line in the angle simplex —\ni.e. along every direction `(u,v,w)` with `u+v+w = 0` that is not zero.\n\nSince strict concavity on a convex set is exactly strict concavity along every\nsegment, this is Rivin's theorem for a single tetrahedron. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:rivin-concavity-one-tetrahedron","label":"thm:rivin-concavity-one-tetrahedron","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/rivin-concavity-one-tetrahedron.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.deriv2_tetVolLine_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.deriv2_tetVolLine_neg","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L353-L404","doc":"**The second derivative along the line is `−cotQuadratic`, hence negative.**\nThis is where `Λ″ = −cot` and `cot_quadratic_pos` meet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_tetVolLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_tetVolLine","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L331-L351","doc":"First derivative along the line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.tetLine_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.tetLine_sum","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L325-L329","doc":"Along the line, the three angles still sum to `π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.convex_tetLineDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.convex_tetLineDomain","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L297-L323","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.tetLineDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.tetLineDomain","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L292-L295","doc":"The admissible parameters: those keeping all three angles positive.  Given\n`α+β+γ = π` and `u+v+w = 0` this also forces each angle `< π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.tetVolLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.tetVolLine","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L286-L290","doc":"The tetrahedron volume `Λ(α)+Λ(β)+Λ(γ)` restricted to the line\n`t ↦ (α+tu, β+tv, γ+tw)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.deriv_deriv_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.deriv_deriv_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L263-L267","doc":"The Hessian entry, in the form `cot_quadratic_pos` consumes: the second\nderivative of `Λ` at an angle is `−cot`, so `−Λ″ = cot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_deriv_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_deriv_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L242-L261","doc":"**`Λ″(t) = −cot t` on `(0, π)`** — bean `qou-mlgp` Gap 2, the analytic input\n`qou-krvm` (iv) was missing.\n\nTogether with `cot_quadratic_pos` this says: the Hessian of `Λ(α)+Λ(β)+Λ(γ)` is\n`diag(−cot α, −cot β, −cot γ)`, and it is negative definite on the tangent space\nof `α+β+γ = π`.  That is Rivin concavity for one ideal tetrahedron.\n\n⚠ Read the sign, and do not generalise it: `−cot` is negative on `(0, π/2)` and\n**positive** on `(π/2, π)`, so `Λ` is concave on the first and **convex** on the\nsecond.  The concavity is a property of the constrained sum, never of `Λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_neg_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_neg_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L226-L240","doc":"`d/dt (−log(2 sin t)) = −cot t` on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.hasDerivAt_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L207-L224","doc":"**`Λ′(t) = −log(2 sin t)` on `(0, π)`.**\n\nChain rule on `Λ(t) = Cl₂(2t)/2` through `hasDerivAt_Cl_2_series`: the factor `2`\nfrom the inner derivative cancels the `/2` in the normalisation, which is exactly\nwhy this normalisation of the Lobachevsky function is the standard one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.cot_quadratic_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.cot_quadratic_pos","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L125-L195","doc":"**Rivin concavity for one ideal tetrahedron** — the Hessian of\n`Λ(α)+Λ(β)+Λ(γ)` is negative definite on the tangent space of the constraint.\n\nGiven positive angles summing to `π` and a tangent vector `u + v + w = 0` that\nis not zero,\n\n    `cot α·u² + cot β·v² + cot γ·w²  >  0`.\n\nNote the hypothesis is `¬(u = 0 ∧ v = 0)`, which under `u + v + w = 0` is\nexactly `(u, v, w) ≠ 0`.\n\nNo case analysis on which angle is obtuse: the sum-of-squares identity absorbs\nit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.cotQuadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.cotQuadratic","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L119-L123","doc":"The quadratic form appearing as `−(Hessian)` of the tetrahedron volume,\nrestricted to the tangent space of `α + β + γ = π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.sin_pos_of_sum_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.sin_pos_of_sum_pi","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L112-L117","doc":"Every angle of a \"triangle\" (three positive reals summing to `π`) is `< π`,\nso its sine is positive.  Stated for the first slot; apply with the arguments\npermuted for the others. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Rivin.sos_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Rivin.sos_identity","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/RivinConcavity.lean#L95-L108","doc":"**The identity.**  Clearing the denominators of\n\n    `cot α·u² + cot β·v² + cot γ·w²`   (with `γ = π − α − β`, `w = −(u+v)`)\n\nturns it into a sum of two squares.  Verified symbolically (sympy, exact) before\nbeing stated. ","signatureChunk":0}]}